Based on the code provided, there are three critical issues preventing the Bulk Upload from working:
 * Spring Proxy Bypass (Synchronous Execution): In JournalBulkValidationService, you are calling the @Async method processAsync directly from initiateValidation within the same class. This bypasses Spring's proxy, causing the method to run synchronously (blocking the main thread). The UI freezes waiting for the whole file to process instead of getting an immediate Request ID.
 * Missing Async Configuration: You are using @Async("bulkExecutor"), but there is no configuration defining a thread pool named bulkExecutor. Spring will throw an exception or fail to initialize the async context.
 * Frontend Content-Type Issue: In JournalBulkUpload.js, you are explicitly sending "multipart/form-data" to your custom hook. When sending FormData, the browser must set the Content-Type automatically to include the boundary. Manually setting it breaks the payload, and the backend receives an empty file.
Here are the optimized, corrected files.
